# CoinCync — code ownership for review-gated paths.
#
# This project now has three maintainers. @ghostrider1092 is the lead and
# default owner; @junbyjun1238 and @0x4D-5A are co-owners on the review-gated
# code paths below (consensus, crypto, wallet, mempool + network, rpc, and the
# consensus-integrity lock), so a change on any of those auto-requests review
# from all three and an inflation / privacy / consensus bug can't land without
# a second pair of eyes review-gated by code-owner association. The governance
# docs (Constitution / threat model / KNOWN_ISSUES) stay with the lead.
#
# When git.coincync.network goes live, this file becomes the single
# source of truth Forgejo's branch protection reads.
#
# Operational roles (release manager, fleet operator, security inbox,
# etc.) that don't map to a code path live in /MAINTAINERS.md instead.
# When a backup is named there, add the same handle to the relevant
# row(s) below so GitHub auto-requests review from all owners. The "Two-of-N
# maintainer sign-offs for consensus rules" rule in CONTRIBUTING.md is now
# enforceable: the consensus paths carry three owners, so branch protection
# can require two approving reviews on consensus paths — tighten it to do so
# when the forge supports it.
#
# Bus-factor inventory + recovery procedure:
#   /docs/governance/bus-factor.md
#   /docs/operations/MAINTAINER_RECOVERY.md

# Default owner (catches everything not matched below).
*                                   @ghostrider1092

# ── Consensus paths: any change here can fork the chain ─────────────
# Block validation, tx validation, supply emission curve, reorg policy,
# difficulty adjustment, the constants file. A bug in any of these is
# usually unrecoverable without coordinated rollback.
/src/consensus/                     @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A
/src/transaction/validator.rs       @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A
/src/chain.rs                       @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A
/src/emission.rs                    @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A
/src/constants.rs                   @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A

# ── Cryptographic primitives: any change here can break privacy ─────
# CLSAG, Bulletproofs+, stealth-address derivation, key-image
# computation, Pedersen commitments. Bugs here are silent: a tx looks
# valid but leaks linkage to chain analysts, or worse, allows
# inflation via crafted range proofs.
/src/crypto/                        @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A

# ── Wallet send + scan: any change here can lose user funds ─────────
# Tx-build path: ring selection, decoy logic, fee math, change
# computation, in-flight reservation tracking. Scan path: spent
# detection, output decryption, balance updates. Bugs here can
# produce silent double-spends or stuck UTXOs.
/src/wallet/send.rs                 @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A
/src/wallet/scanner.rs              @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A
/src/wallet/balance.rs              @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A
/src/bin/wallet.rs                  @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A

# ── Mempool + network admit paths: chain-stall vectors ──────────────
# A bug in tx-admit that lets invalid txs persist will stall block
# production (the 2026-05-07 "shadow conflict" stalls are the
# canonical example).
/src/mempool.rs                     @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A
/src/network/                       @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A

# ── RPC surface: anything user-facing or attack-surface ─────────────
# REST proxy, JSON-RPC server, allowlist gating. Mistakes here can
# expose write methods publicly or leak privacy-relevant stats
# (Item 5 in the 2026-05-07 review).
/src/rpc/                           @ghostrider1092 @junbyjun1238 @0x4D-5A

# ── Constitution + threat model + KNOWN_ISSUES ──────────────────────
# These are the contract with users. Edits should be deliberate and
# stay with the lead maintainer.
/CONSTITUTION.md                    @ghostrider1092
/docs/THREAT_MODEL.md               @ghostrider1092
/docs/launch/KNOWN_ISSUES.md        @ghostrider1092

